## Context

The finance ledger does not say whether the money moves steel. Operations
are attached to plants, lines, storage, renewable capacity and social
measures, so as to measure delays, MW closed or commissioned, and the
coexistence of the partnerships with new fossil assets. Milestone M3b of
[[0725]].

Normative text, accepted specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):
`docs/jetp-requirements.md` F20 (finance joined to assets, M3b);
`docs/jetp-fusion.md` § 3 (identity judgements) and § 5; the asset and party
classes of `docs/jetp-ontology.md`; storage targets in [[1872]].

## Test

An operation joins an asset only by a stable identifier or a documented
judgement (F20). The cases Komati, Cirebon-1, Bac Ai and Vung Ang II must
show the four states: an effective closure, a retirement cancelled or
reassigned, low-carbon infrastructure under construction, and a new fossil
asset commissioned during the partnership.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An asset register distinct from the finance ledger
- [ ] Each join is a stable identifier or a judgement with stance, likelihood, confidence and basis under fusion § 3, with its source statements
- [ ] The chronology from financing to realisation can be reconstructed, and the four cases above are represented correctly
- [ ] First dollars-per-MW and delay indicators produced, with their limits stated
